  "decision_conditions": [
    "The information submitted for Condition 6 (Structural Method Statement) is incomplete, lacking a required drainage survey and is insufficient to discharge the condition and to demonstrate that the character and appearance of the Listed Structure would be safeguarded. As such, the submission fails to  comply with Policy HC1 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CS8 of the Core Strategy (2012), and Policies DM10 and DM12 of the LDF Core Strategy (2012).",
    "The submission includes proposed structural works to the roof that were not granted consent as part of Listed Building Consent 22/01927/LBC. A discharge of condition application cannot be used to make any additional changes or variations to the original Listed Building Consent. A new Listed Building Consent is required. Accordingly, the merits of these additional works have not been assessed by Officers and no approval can be inferred by the applicant. The proposals are therefore contrary to the provisions of The Planning (Listed Building And Conservation Areas) Act 1990 (as amended) and The Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) England) Order 2015 (as amended)."
  ],
